{"id": "section-body-24017", "title": "Endometrial Cancer", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-two", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MALIGNANT DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Gynecological Malignancies", "Endometrial Cancer"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-24017", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Endometrial Cancer", "runs": [{"text": "Endometrial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cancer"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "534"}}, {"id": "body-24018", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is predominantly a disease of old women. Traditionally, EC is classified into Type I (estrogen-related, precursor: atypical endometrial hyperplasia) and Type II (de novo, i.e., due to mutations, no precursor). Type I includes endometrioid (most common), while other histologies are classified as type II (serous, clear cell carcinoma, and mucinous adenocarcinoma).", "runs": [{"text": "This is predominantly a disease of old women. Traditionally, EC is classified into Type I (estrogen-related, precursor: atypical endometrial hyperplasia) and Type II (de novo, i.e., due to mutations, no precursor). Type I includes endometrioid (most common), while other histologies are classified as type II (serous, clear cell carcinoma, and mucinous adenocarcinoma)."}]}, {"id": "body-24020", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Risk factors", "runs": [{"text": "Risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "factors"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-24021", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Risk factors for endometrial carcinoma include high BMI, hyperinsulinemia (diabetes), prolonged exposure to unopposed estrogen (often related to nulliparity and infertility associated with PCOS or tamoxifen use, early age at menarche, and late age at menopause), and hypertension.", "runs": [{"text": "Risk factors for endometrial carcinoma include high BMI, hyperinsulinemia (diabetes), prolonged exposure to unopposed estrogen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "related"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nulliparity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infertility"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PCOS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tamoxifen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "early"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "age"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "menarche,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "late"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "age at menopause), and hypertension."}]}, {"id": "body-24024", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-24025", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Abnormal uterine bleeding, especially in postmenopausal women. The bleeding can be persistent intermenstrual bleeding or irregular or infrequent heavy bleeding in women who are obese/PCOS or those using tamoxifen", "runs": [{"text": "Abnormal uterine bleeding, especially in postmenopausal women. The bleeding can be persistent intermenstrual bleeding or irregular or infrequent heavy bleeding in women who are obese/PCOS or those using tamoxifen"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "487"}}, {"id": "body-24026", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Vaginal discharge", "runs": [{"text": "Vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discharge"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "487"}}, {"id": "body-24027", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Thickened endometrium incidentally noted on USS for other condition", "runs": [{"text": "Thickened"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "endometrium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "incidentally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "noted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "USS for 